const LESSONS = {"AI Fundamentals":["The big picture","AI is the broad field. Machine learning learns patterns from data; deep learning uses multi-layer neural networks; generative AI creates new content. Training learns parameters; inference uses the trained model."],"Agents, Search & Planning":["How an AI system chooses","An agent observes an environment and chooses actions. Search represents a problem as states, actions and goals. BFS explores by depth, DFS follows a branch, and informed methods use heuristics; A* combines cost so far with estimated remaining cost."],"Knowledge & Uncertainty":["Reasoning when facts are incomplete","Knowledge representation stores facts and relationships. Inference derives conclusions. Probability represents uncertainty, and Bayesian reasoning updates beliefs when new evidence arrives."],"Machine Learning Foundations":["How models learn","Supervised learning uses labeled targets; unsupervised learning finds structure without labels. Features are inputs. Training fits the model, validation guides choices, and the test set estimates final performance on unseen data."],"Core ML Models":["Match the method to the problem","Classification predicts categories, regression predicts numbers, and clustering finds groups. Decision trees split on features, k-NN uses nearby examples, ensembles combine models, and k-means forms clusters."],"Evaluation & Generalization":["Know what “good” means","Accuracy is overall correctness. Precision asks how many predicted positives were truly positive; recall asks how many actual positives were found. F1 balances precision and recall. Watch for overfitting, leakage and class imbalance."],"Neural Networks & Deep Learning":["The learning loop","Neural networks combine weighted inputs through layers and nonlinear activations. A forward pass makes a prediction; loss measures error; backpropagation computes gradients; gradient descent updates weights."],"NLP, Transformers & LLMs":["How modern language AI works","Text is tokenized and represented with embeddings. Transformers use attention to relate parts of the context. LLMs generate likely next tokens. RAG adds retrieved information; fine-tuning changes model parameters; hallucinations are plausible but unsupported outputs."],"Reinforcement Learning":["Learning from consequences","An agent acts in an environment and receives rewards. A policy maps states or observations to actions. Learning balances exploration of uncertain actions with exploitation of actions already believed to work well."],"Responsible AI":["Useful AI must also be trustworthy","Real systems need appropriate data, fairness checks, privacy and security, transparency, robustness, human oversight and monitoring. Strong average accuracy does not guarantee safe or fair performance in every group or situation."]};

const DATA = { questions: QUESTIONS, lessons: LESSONS };
